{"type": "message", "id": "db0d545b", "parentId": "8e393999", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:32:33.075Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:5", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"exoplanet high eccentricity radial velocity discovered before 2020 super Earth 5 Earth masses\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1084,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"09e74ac5cebce589\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuper-Earth - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"09e74ac5cebce589\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super-Earth\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba01a2dac3b3de40\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe planet has a minimum mass <strong>3.1 times that of Earth</strong> and a nearly circular orbit at 0.146 AU with a period of 36.6 days, placing it in the middle of the habitable zone where liquid water could exist and midway between the planets c and d. It was discovered using the radial velocity method ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba01a2dac3b3de40\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"6 days ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d0ee431653f020c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanets detected by radial velocity - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d0ee431653f020c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanets_detected_by_radial_velocity\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c35e8c459ca0411b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most massive exoplanet candidate is HD 217786 b, which masses <strong>12.98 MJ</strong>; the least massive confirmed planet is HD 10180 b, which masses 0.004 MJ or 3.1 M🜨. The longest period of any confirmed exoplanet is 47 Ursae Majoris d, which takes 14002 days or 38.33 years to make one trip around ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c35e8c459ca0411b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 3, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7e14751530546842\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n55 Cancri Ae - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7e14751530546842\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/55_Cancri_Ae\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4bea0f27bc48a21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLike the majority of extrasolar planets found prior to the Kepler mission, <strong>55 Cancri Ae</strong> was discovered by detecting variations in its star&#x27;s radial velocity. This was achieved by making sensitive measurements of the Doppler shift of the spectrum of 55 Cancri A. At the time of its discovery, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f4bea0f27bc48a21\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 21, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5830cd9b3c06d6a5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGiant Outer Transiting Exoplanet Mass (GOT ‘EM) Survey. II. Discovery of a Failed Hot Jupiter on a 2.7 Yr, Highly Eccentric Orbit* | Request PDF\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5830cd9b3c06d6a5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354732066_Giant_Outer_Transiting_Exoplanet_Mass_GOT_'EM_Survey_II_Discovery_of_a_Failed_Hot_Jupiter_on_a_27_Yr_Highly_Eccentric_Orbit\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"862bf3afeb5c8d69\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUsing long term radial velocity monitoring, we measure the mass of the gas giant Kepler-167e (P = 1071 days) to be <strong>1.01^(+0.16)_(−0.15) M_J</strong>, thus confirming it as a Jupiter analog.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"862bf3afeb5c8d69\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 1, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f032245934cce509\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA hidden 'super-Earth' exoplanet is dipping in and out of its habitable zone | Space\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f032245934cce509\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.space.com/astronomy/exoplanets/a-hidden-super-earth-exoplanet-is-dipping-in-and-out-of-its-habitable-zone\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a587b097cb2eb9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAnd, unlike radial velocity and transit measurements, which tend to be biased toward finding short-period exoplanets, TTVs open a window onto planets on wider orbits that are not seen to transit. &quot;[Kepler-725c&#x27;s discovery] demonstrates the potential of the TTV technique to detect low-mass planets in habitable zones of sun-like stars,&quot; said Sun.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8a587b097cb2eb9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 6, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.space.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0e68e8fbbc1c64b0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0e68e8fbbc1c64b0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/539/2/727/8098228\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7eb9edf9dd36ecd3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe eccentricity distribution of exoplanets is also inherently linked to the masses of planets themselves. Small planets in multiple systems are likely to have smaller eccentricities (e.g. Van Eylen &amp; Albrecht 2015; Xie et al. 2016; Van Eylen et al. 2019), whereas giant planets in wide orbits overwhelmingly exhibit larger eccentricities (Bitsch, Trifonov &amp; Izidoro 2020, and references therein). To investigate the distinction between low (super-Earths), moderate (Neptune-type planets), and high-mass planets (gas giants, like the gaseous giant planets of the Solar system), we have split our sample into three mass bins.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7eb9edf9dd36ecd3\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 12, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5ec4e57c4ce0f19\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanet extremes - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5ec4e57c4ce0f19\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanet_extremes\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"377081d6665869b5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe following are lists of extremes among the known exoplanets. The properties listed here are those for which values are known reliably. The study of exoplanets is one of the most dynamic emerging fields of science, thus these values may change as new discoveries are made.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"377081d6665869b5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"1 month ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbbe1e042ac0dccb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbbe1e042ac0dccb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.20385\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9400d6bd4e9e9915\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHelp | Advanced Search · arXiv is a free distribution service and an open-access archive for nearly 2.4 million scholarly articles in the fields of physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative finance, statistics, electrical engineering and systems science, and ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9400d6bd4e9e9915\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"afc742d7c0d20d23\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExoplanets Catalogue Analysis: The Distribution of Exoplanets at FGK Stars by Mass and Orbital Period Accounting for the Observational Selection in the Radial Velocity Method | MDPI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"afc742d7c0d20d23\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4433/14/2/353\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"971f93cd1e987fab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhen considering exoplanets discovered ... the RV exoplanets approximately follows to a piecewise power law with the breaks at <strong>~0.14 and ~1.7 MJ</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"971f93cd1e987fab\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdpi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32922c85df56084f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nr/space on Reddit: ‘Super-Earth’ discovered — and it’s a prime candidate for alien life\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32922c85df56084f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/space/comments/1ibydxw/superearth_discovered_and_its_a_prime_candidate/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27ba8ca4954650c2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis &quot;super-Earth,&quot; <strong>approximately six times the mass of our planet</strong>, orbits within the habitable zone of its star, HD 20794, where conditions may allow for liquid water—a crucial ingredient for life.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27ba8ca4954650c2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 28, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.reddit.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "exoplanet high eccentricity radial velocity discovered before 2020 super Earth 5 Earth masses", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1084, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"09e74ac5cebce589\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSuper-Earth - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"09e74ac5cebce589\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super-Earth", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba01a2dac3b3de40\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe planet has a minimum mass <strong>3.1 times that of Earth</strong> and a nearly circular orbit at 0.146 AU with a period of 36.6 days, placing it in the middle of the habitable zone where liquid water could exist and midway between the planets c and d. It was discovered using the radial velocity method ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba01a2dac3b3de40\">>>", "published": "6 days ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d0ee431653f020c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nList of exoplanets detected by radial velocity - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d0ee431653f020c\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanets_detected_by_radial_velocity", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c35e8c459ca0411b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe most massive exoplanet candidate is HD 217786 b, which masses <strong>12.98 MJ</strong>; the least massive confirmed planet is HD 10180 b, which masses 0.004 MJ or 3.1 M🜨. The longest period of any confirmed exoplanet is 47 Ursae Majoris d, which takes 14002 days or 38.33 years to make one trip around ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c35e8c459ca0411b\">>>", "published": "December 3, 2024", "siteName": "