{"type": "message", "id": "16fc4e2e", "parentId": "c57d3acb", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:32:46.307Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:9", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"exoplanet radial velocity high eccentricity 0.4 0.5 0.6 discovered before 2020 super Earth 5 Earth masses\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1059,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f05de13be6e2ccaf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanets detected by radial velocity - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f05de13be6e2ccaf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanets_detected_by_radial_velocity\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d0c20d57f83aad6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe following is a list of 456 extrasolar planets that were only detected by radial velocity method –– 31 confirmed and 323 candidates, sorted by orbital periods. Since none of these planets are transiting or directly observed, they do not have measured radii and generally their masses ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d0c20d57f83aad6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 3, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3327b96d2ed98966\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n55 Cancri Ae - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3327b96d2ed98966\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/55_Cancri_Ae\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"062d8ce54ca44134\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLike the majority of extrasolar planets found prior to the Kepler mission, <strong>55 Cancri Ae</strong> was discovered by detecting variations in its star&#x27;s radial velocity. This was achieved by making sensitive measurements of the Doppler shift of the spectrum of 55 Cancri A. At the time of its discovery, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"062d8ce54ca44134\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 21, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"423d80a004b1a721\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanet extremes - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"423d80a004b1a721\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanet_extremes\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8cda0b8af2fb9dd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe following are lists of extremes among the known exoplanets. The properties listed here are those for which values are known reliably. The study of exoplanets is one of the most dynamic emerging fields of science, thus these values may change as new discoveries are made.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8cda0b8af2fb9dd\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"1 month ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fae492504af8462c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fae492504af8462c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/539/2/727/8098228\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1e65e80bc6fa031\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis aligns with what one would expect when calculating the average reported eccentricity for planets in each mass bin: |$\\\\overline{e}=0.164,0.191,0.245$|⁠, in order of increasing mass. The preference for local fits provides overwhelming evidence that mass is also a key factor sculpting the eccentricity distribution. This will however also be coupled to the period distribution, due to the detection sensitivity of our instruments and the currently known catalogue of exoplanets showing clusters of detections in the cold-Jupiter or hot/warm super-Earth regimes (see Section 5.2.4 and Fig.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d1e65e80bc6fa031\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 12, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"316064785276d55a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGiant Outer Transiting Exoplanet Mass (GOT ‘EM) Survey. II. Discovery of a Failed Hot Jupiter on a 2.7 Yr, Highly Eccentric Orbit* | Request PDF\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"316064785276d55a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354732066_Giant_Outer_Transiting_Exoplanet_Mass_GOT_'EM_Survey_II_Discovery_of_a_Failed_Hot_Jupiter_on_a_27_Yr_Highly_Eccentric_Orbit\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"539d2442b753c38b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis supports the hypothesis that dynamical interactions with wide stellar companions plays an important role in the formation of highly eccentric exoplanets. ... Paul A. Dalba · Heather A. Knutson ... The observed correlation between outer giant planets and inner super-Earths is emerging as an important constraint on planet formation theories. In this study we focus on Kepler-167, which is currently the only system known to contain both inner transiting super-Earths and a confirmed outer transiting gas giant companion beyond 1 au. Using long term radial velocity monitoring, we measure the mass of the gas giant Kepler-167e (P = 1071 days) to be 1.01^(+0.16)_(−0.15) M_J, thus confirming it as a Jupiter analog.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"539d2442b753c38b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 1, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a8d92e791eb1c12\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuper-Earth - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a8d92e791eb1c12\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super-Earth\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2915782509e1a20d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe planet has a <strong>minimum mass 3.1 times that of Earth</strong> and a nearly circular orbit at 0.146 AU with a period of 36.6 days, placing it in the middle of the habitable zone where liquid water could exist and midway between the planets c and d. It ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2915782509e1a20d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"6 days ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05f21bbec6fd8323\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExoplanets Catalogue Analysis: The Distribution of Exoplanets at FGK Stars by Mass and Orbital Period Accounting for the Observational Selection in the Radial Velocity Method | MDPI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05f21bbec6fd8323\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4433/14/2/353\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c41629942f8ca0d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhen considering exoplanets discovered ... the RV exoplanets approximately follows to a piecewise power law with the breaks at <strong>~0.14 and ~1.7 MJ</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c41629942f8ca0d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdpi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0fd2671a7c0aa8e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDiscoveries of exoplanets - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f0fd2671a7c0aa8e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": 