 mass 3.1 times that of Earth</strong> and a nearly circular orbit at 0.146 AU with a period of 36.6 days, placing it in the middle of the habitable zone where liquid water could exist and midway between the planets c and d. It ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2915782509e1a20d\">>>", "published": "6 days ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05f21bbec6fd8323\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExoplanets Catalogue Analysis: The Distribution of Exoplanets at FGK Stars by Mass and Orbital Period Accounting for the Observational Selection in the Radial Velocity Method | MDPI\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"05f21bbec6fd8323\">>>", "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4433/14/2/353", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4c41629942f8ca0d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWhen considering exoplanets discovered ... the RV exoplanets approximately follows to a piecewise power law with the breaks at <strong>~0.14 and ~1.7 MJ</strong>....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4c41629942f8ca0d\">>>", "published": "February 10, 2023", "siteName": "www.mdpi.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f0fd2671a7c0aa8e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDiscoveries of exoplanets - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f0fd2671a7c0aa8e\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discoveries_of_exoplanets", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50573e36f73c6b90\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn 7 June, scientists working at ... at a distance of 600 light-years from Earth, the exoplanet has a mass <strong>27 times heavier than that of Earth</strong> and is 6 times its radius....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50573e36f73c6b90\">>>", "published": "2 weeks ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"371c8ffc1d597aae\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHigher water loss on Earth-like exoplanets in eccentric orbits | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"371c8ffc1d597aae\">>>", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/524/1/1491/7199796", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef8b0093c3f0ab27\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo date, <strong>GJ 1061 d</strong>, a potentially rocky exoplanet (&gt;1.5 M⊕) detected by the radial velocity method, has the largest constrained eccentricity (e &lt; 0.54; Dreizler et al. 2020). The 10 M⊕ sets the boundary between super-Earth and ice/gas giant ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ef8b0093c3f0ab27\">>>", "published": "July 4, 2023", "siteName": "academic.oup.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a418e912e8fb5b60\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nInstituto de Astrofísica e Ciências do Espaço\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a418e912e8fb5b60\">>>", "url": "https://www.iastro.pt/research/paperDetails.html?ID=3040", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"feec5aa0cbcca158\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFurther analysis of these RVs reveals the presence of an additional planet, <strong>HD 35843 b</strong>, with a period of 9.90 days and a minimum mass of 5.84 ± 0.84 M⊕. For HD 35843 c, a joint photometric and spectroscopic analysis yields a radius of 2.54 ± 0.08 R⊕, a mass of 11.32 ± 1.60 M⊕, and ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"feec5aa0cbcca158\">>>", "siteName": "www.iastro.pt"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775298766306}}
