nce the planets were detected by the radial velocity ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc34bcb067467ff1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 17, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74eb982854f84299\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 1061 c - NASA Science\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"74eb982854f84299\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanet-catalog/gj-1061-c/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f21fe839690d4a6f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 1061 c is a super Earth exoplanet that orbits an M-type star. Its mass is 1.74 Earths, it takes 6.7 days to complete one orbit of its star, and is 0.035 AU from its star. <strong>Its discovery was announced in 2020.</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f21fe839690d4a6f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"3 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"science.nasa.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b6ce773a8c04d1e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 1061 b - NASA Science\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2b6ce773a8c04d1e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanet-catalog/gj-1061-b/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e05de6f4d427c6c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 1061 b is a super Earth exoplanet that orbits an M-type star. Its mass is 1.37 Earths, it takes 3.2 days to complete one orbit of its star, and is 0.021 AU from its star. <strong>Its discovery was announced in 2020.</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e05de6f4d427c6c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"March 6, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"science.nasa.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05d3aee23714ca75\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHabitable Planet Reality Check: The Nearby GJ 1061 | Drew Ex Machina\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"05d3aee23714ca75\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.drewexmachina.com/2019/08/21/habitable-planet-reality-check-the-nearby-gj-1061/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b24d5f4660f2de1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe <strong>ESO 3.6m Telescope equipped with the HARPS spectrograph was used to acquire data used to search for new exoplanets orbiting nearby stars like GJ 1061. (ESO/H.H.Heyer) Because of its low level of stellar activity, GJ 1061 is considered a good target for searches using precision radial velocity (RV) measurements to detect the reflex motion of orbiting planets especially those with short periods</strong>...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6b24d5f4660f2de1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 22, 2019\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.drewexmachina.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81023445c5fa6caf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThree super-Earths discovered in the GJ 1061 red dwarf system\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81023445c5fa6caf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://english.tachyonbeam.com/2019/09/04/three-super-earths-discovered-in-the-gj-1061-red-dwarf-system/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2626823c67244d10\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis project uses the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the <strong>La Silla Observatory in Chile</strong>. These are surveys that use the radial velocity method to discover traces of exoplanets and in the GJ 1061 system the detections carried out between July and September ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2626823c67244d10\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 4, 2019\",\n      \"siteName\": \"english.tachyonbeam.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22b98febbdbc2aca\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpen Exoplanet Catalogue - GJ 1061 d\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"22b98febbdbc2aca\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.openexoplanetcatalogue.com/planet/GJ%201061%20d/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8d6e9e7b91073056\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe planetary system GJ 1061 hosts at least 3 planets · This list shows all planetary and stellar components in the system. It gives a quick overview of the hierarchical architecture\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8d6e9e7b91073056\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.openexoplanetcatalogue.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a053716408c4c6a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 1061 | NASA Exoplanet Archive\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a053716408c4c6a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/overview/GJ1061\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa13df2a54094660\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>RedDots</strong>: a temperate 1.5 Earth-mass planet candidate in a compact multiterrestrial planet system around GJ 1061 Dreizler et al.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa13df2a54094660\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"760dd671684b2ebd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAstronomy:GJ 1061 - HandWiki\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"760dd671684b2ebd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://handwiki.org/wiki/Astronomy:GJ_1061_c\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5684e4be0e119f6b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOn August 13, 2019, a planetary system was announced orbiting the star GJ 1061 by the Red Dots project for detecting terrestrial planets around nearby red dwarf stars.[7] The planet GJ 1061 d orbits in the conservative circumstellar habitable zone of its star and the planet GJ 1061 c orbits in the inner edge of the habitable zone.[7] GJ 1061 is a non-variable star that does not suffer flares, so there is a greater probability that the exoplanets still conserve their atmosphere if they had one.[9]\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5684e4be0e119f6b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 17, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"handwiki.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54e4115b9e17b426\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGravity Simulator | GJ 1061 - System With 3 Exoplanets of Which 1 Is Potentially Habitable\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54e4115b9e17b426\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://gravitysimulator.org/exoplanets/gj-1061-system-with-3-exoplanets-of-which-1-is-potentially-habitable/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af05f470aa55e2fc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n3D visualisation and gravity simulation of the exoplanet system GJ 1061, which contains 3 exoplanets, of which 1 is potentially habitable, and was discovered by the <strong>La Silla Observatory</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af05f470aa55e2fc\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"gravitysimulator.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "GJ 1061 d exoplanet eccentricity radial velocity discovery facility", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 881, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e9e0ddf7133772ea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGJ 1061 d - NASA Science\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e9e0ddf7133772ea\">>>", "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanet-catalog/gj-1061-d/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dc29b5837b4cc10b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGJ 1061 d is a super Earth exoplanet that orbits an M-type star. Its mass is 1.64 Earths, it takes 13 days to complete one orbit of i