"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6ebed03da68603f5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 d - NASA Science\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6ebed03da68603f5\">>>", "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanet-catalog/hd-20794-d/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cd9e51a7ca11e55\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 d is a super Earth exoplanet that orbits a G-type star. Its mass is 4.8 Earths, it takes 90.3 days to complete one orbit of its star, and is 0.3499 AU from its star. <strong>Its discovery was announced in 2011.</strong>\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cd9e51a7ca11e55\">>>", "published": "February 13, 2026", "siteName": "science.nasa.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c123591544935c3d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 d\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c123591544935c3d\">>>", "url": "http://www.exoplanetkyoto.org/exohtml/HD_20794_d.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6004b2904c59c8aa\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDisplay orbital revolution of HD 20794 d around the hoststar HD 20794\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6004b2904c59c8aa\">>>", "siteName": "www.exoplanetkyoto.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"377cecca53a891ac\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRevisiting the Multi-planetary System of the Nearby star HD 20794: Confirmation of a Low-mass Planet in the Habitable Zone of a Nearby G-dwarf - Astrobiology\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"377cecca53a891ac\">>>", "url": "https://astrobiology.com/2025/02/revisiting-the-multi-planetary-system-of-the-nearby-star-hd-20794-confirmation-of-a-low-mass-planet-in-the-habitable-zone-of-a-nearby-g-dwarf.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cdfb7b452eaae3d3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTESS target pixel file for HD 20794. No nearby sources are detected by the Gaia DR3 catalog up to a contrast magnitude of +6 within the TESS aperture. — — astro-ph.EP · Close-by Earth analogs and super-Earths are of primary importance because they will be preferential targets for the next generation of direct imaging instruments. Bright and close-by G-to-M type stars are preferential targets in radial velocity surveys to find Earth analogs.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cdfb7b452eaae3d3\">>>", "published": "February 4, 2025", "siteName": "astrobiology.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"200f21a624dfface\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 | NASA Exoplanet Archive\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"200f21a624dfface\">>>", "url": "https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/overview/HD%2020794", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad922eedc8153785\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRevisiting the multi-planetary system of the nearby star HD 20794: Confirmation of a low-mass planet in the habitable zone of a nearby G-dwarf Nari et al. 2025 | Reference Overview · Doppler Constraints on Planetary Companions to Nearby Sun-like Stars: An Archival Radial Velocity Survey of Southern Targets for Proposed NASA Direct Imaging Missions Laliotis et al.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad922eedc8153785\">>>", "siteName": "exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f62035ac6263ad2a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe exoplanet HD 20794 d has a highly elliptical orbit that is only partly in the habitable zone.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f62035ac6263ad2a\">>>", "url": "https://english.tachyonbeam.com/2025/02/04/the-exoplanet-hd-20794-d-has-a-highly-elliptical-orbit-that-is-only-partly-in-the-habitable-zone/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35cdf2fa04b734cc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA team of researchers used data collected in more than twenty years with two spectrographs: ESPRESSO, mounted on the VLT, and HARPS, at the <strong>La Silla Observatory</strong>, both of ESO in Chile, to identify HD 20794 d and define its orbit and characteristics.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"35cdf2fa04b734cc\">>>", "siteName": "english.tachyonbeam.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775298778175}}
