than 0.03 AU and has a minimum mass estimated at 1.9 times that of Earth. As of January 2010, this is the lightest known extrasolar planet to orbit a main-sequence star. 30 planets: On October 19, it was announced that 30 new planets were discovered, all were detected by the radial velocity method. It is the most planets ever announced in a single day during the exoplanet ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba186ad2dbe55265\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"2 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34372c29bee26f61\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34372c29bee26f61\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/539/2/727/8098228\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6c1bf3f27b6edbb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe examine the eccentricity distribution(s) of radial velocity (RV) detected exoplanets. Previously, the eccentricity distribution was found to be described well by a Beta distribution with shape parameters |$a=0.867\\\\,\\\\mathrm{ and}\\\\, b=3.03$|⁠. Increasing the sample size by a factor of 2.25, we find that the cumulative distribution function regression method now prefers a mixture model of Rayleigh + Exponential distributions over the Beta distribution, with an increase in Bayesian evidence of |$\\\\Delta \\\\ln {Z}\\\\sim 77$| (⁠|$12.6\\\\, \\\\sigma$|⁠).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6c1bf3f27b6edbb\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 12, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"02bab705ac4b21b6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nradial velocity exoplanet: Topics by Science.gov\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"02bab705ac