{"type": "message", "id": "16dbd55c", "parentId": "c45e0b1e", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:33:17.747Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:14", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"HD 20794 d eccentricity 0.40 HARPS La Silla Chile\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1064,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d858e1fdc9097a1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRevisiting the multi-planetary system of the nearby star HD 20794 - Confirmation of a low-mass planet in the habitable zone of a nearby G-dwarf | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9d858e1fdc9097a1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2025/01/aa51769-24/aa51769-24.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"162fd76887a26a40\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHowever, nightly stacking does not reduce the instrumental noise on a timescale beyond the intra-night timescale. Due to the brightness of HD 20794, we used short exposure times of 60 seconds. HARPS (Mayor et al. 2003) is <strong>a fiber-fed spectrograph installed at the Observatory of La Silla, in Chile</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"162fd76887a26a40\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 28, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aanda.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"075e332b3868d605\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe exoplanet HD 20794 d has a highly elliptical orbit that is only partly in the habitable zone.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"075e332b3868d605\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://english.tachyonbeam.com/2025/02/04/the-exoplanet-hd-20794-d-has-a-highly-elliptical-orbit-that-is-only-partly-in-the-habitable-zone/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63657ceb17e4a6c2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAn article published in the journal “Astronomy &amp; Astrophysics” reports the identification of the exoplanet that was cataloged as HD 20794 d. A team of researchers used data collected in more than twenty years with two spectrographs: ESPRESSO, mounted on the VLT, and HARPS, at the La Silla Observatory, both of ESO in Chile, to identify HD 20794 d and define its orbit and characteristics.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63657ceb17e4a6c2\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"english.tachyonbeam.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8a28a4d5aba6f203\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExoplanet HD 20794 d in the habitable zone | BBC Sky at Night Magazine\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8a28a4d5aba6f203\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.skyatnightmagazine.com/news/hd-20794-d\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3990c4f6d8a65ba9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nESO&#x27;s La Silla observatory in the Chilean Atacama Desert. Credit: Y. Beletsky (LCO)/ESO · Dr Michael Cretignier from the University of Oxford in the UK first discovered the exoplanet candidate that would later be confirmed as HD 20794 d. He was analysing archive data recorded by the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3990c4f6d8a65ba9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 29, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.skyatnightmagazine.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34b69b9b87e285b7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSearch for life: This newly discovered super Earth outside our solar system marks a significant milestone - BusinessToday\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"34b69b9b87e285b7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.businesstoday.in/science/story/search-for-life-this-newly-discovered-super-earth-outside-our-solar-system-marks-a-significant-milestone-463951-2025-02-09\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0014e89da42f2ab9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHD 20794 d, with a mass six times that of Earth, <strong>orbits a star similar to our sun</strong>. The planet’s location within the habitable zone — where conditions may allow liquid water to exist — offers scientists a compelling target for future ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0014e89da42f2ab9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.businesstoday.in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1188482a4870a7be\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExistence Of Exoplanet HD 20794 d In A Habitable Zone Confirmed - Astrobiology\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1188482a4870a7be\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://astrobiology.com/2025/01/existence-of-exoplanet-hd-20794-d-in-a-habitable-zone-confirmed.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8f39e7835c1dae2e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Dr Michael Cretignier first identified a candidate exoplanet signal in 2022</strong>, while analysing archived data recorded by the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8f39e7835c1dae2e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 28, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"astrobiology.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4dd43d7eddffcb07\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvidence for at least three planet candidates orbiting HD 20794 | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4dd43d7eddffcb07\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2017/09/aa30406-17/aa30406-17.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6ae538cc0d09f3c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThere is also weak evidence for the existence of signals at periods of 43 and 11 d. While the 43 d signal does not pass the Bayes factor criterion, the inclusion of this signal in the model can reduce the eccentricity of the 89 d signal. Although the 11 d signal only increases the Bayes factor by a factor of about 20, it consistently appears in different data chunks. Thus by applying noise modeling to the P11 and newer HARPS data, we confirm the two candidates at periods of 18 and 90 d reported by P11 and quantify them better. But we are suspicious about the existence of the reported 40 d candidate because it does not pass the signal detection criteria.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e6ae538cc0d09f3c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 18, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aanda.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"931f540cc80544d7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGravity Simulator | HD 20794 - System With 4 Exoplanets\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"931f540cc80544d7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://gravitysimulator.org/exoplanets/hd-20794-system-with-4-exoplanets/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5ffc2cc3b27fdc0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>3D visualisation and gravity simulation of the exoplanetary system HD 20794, which contains 4 exoplanets and was discovered by the La Silla Observatory</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5ffc2cc3b27fdc0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"gravitysimulator.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43d3cf0c8e551780\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe HARPS search for Earth-like planets in the habitable zone. I. Very low-mass planets around HD 20794, HD 85512, and HD 192310 | Request PDF\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"43d3cf0c8e551780\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/253183556_The_HARPS_search_for_Earth-like_planets_in_the_habitable_zone_I_Very_low-mass_planets_around_HD_20794_HD_85512_and_HD_192310\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3340d0b368bc880e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>For the outer planet, we find an eccentricity of 0.45 −0.11 +0.10</strong> , whereas the inner planets are compatible with circular orbits. The latter is likely to be a rocky planet in the habitable zone of HD 20794.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3340d0b368bc880e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 21, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8ab8eba02aa5b33\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSuper-Earth found just 20 light-years away is our 'best chance so far' to find life\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f8ab8eba02aa5b33\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.earth.com/news/super-earth-hd-20794-d-found-just-20-light-years-away-is-best-target-yet-for-life/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54e60d0a9b4c652e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOxford University scientist Dr. Michael Cretignier first noticed something unusual in this star’s light while examining archived data from the HARPS spectrograph on the 3.6-meter telescope at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54e60d0a9b4c652e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 30, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.earth.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8e93ce70a3fcbc3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExploring HD 20794 d: A Super-Earth Laboratory for Habitability\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c8e93ce70a3fcbc3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.seti.org/news/exploring-hd-20794-d-a-super-earth-laboratory-for-habitability/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a3575763696657e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThese instruments, used over a period of more than 20 years, allowed astronomers to confirm the presence of HD 20794 d alongside two other planets in the same system. One of the most intriguing aspects of HD 20794 d is its <strong>highly eccentric orbit</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a3575763696657e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 17, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.seti.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "HD 20794 d eccentricity 0.40 HARPS La Silla Chile", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1064, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9d858e1fdc9097a1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRevisiting the multi-planetary system of the nearby star HD 20794 - Confirmation of a low-mass planet in the habitable zone of a nearby G-dwarf | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9d858e1fdc9097a1\">>>", "url": "https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2025/01/aa51769-24/aa51769-24.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"162fd76887a26a40\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHowever, nightly stacking does not reduce the instrumental noise on a timescale beyond the intra-night timescale. Due to the brightness of HD 20794, we used short exposure times of 60 seconds. HARPS (Mayor et al. 2003) is <strong>a fiber-fed spectrograph installed at the Observatory of La Silla, in Chile</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"162fd76887a26a40\">>>", "published": "January 28, 2025", "siteName": "www.aanda.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"075e332b3868d605\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe exoplanet HD 20794 d has a highly elliptical orbit that is only partly in the habitable zone.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"075e332b3868d605\">>>", "url": "https://english.tachyonbeam.com/2025/02/04/the-exoplanet-hd-20794-d-has-a-highly-elliptical-orbit-that-is-only-partly-in-the-habitable-zone/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"63657ceb17e4a6c2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAn article published in the journal “Astronomy &amp; Astrophysics” reports the identification of the exoplanet that was cataloged as HD 20794 d. A team of researchers used data collected in more than twenty years with two spectrographs: ESPRESSO, mounted on the VLT, and HARPS, at the La Silla Observatory, both of ESO in Chile, to identify HD 20794 d and define its orbit and characteristics.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"63657ceb17e4a6c2\">>>", "siteName": "english.tachyonbeam.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8a28a4d5aba6f203\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExoplanet HD 20794 d in the habitable zone | BBC Sky at Night Magazine\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8a28a4d5aba6f203\">>>", "url": "https://www.skyatnightmagazine.com/news/hd-20794-d", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3990c4f6d8a65ba9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nESO&#x27;s La Silla observatory in the Chilean Atacama Desert. Credit: Y. Beletsky (LCO)/ESO · Dr Michael Cretignier from the University of Oxford in the UK first discovered the exoplanet candidate that would later be confirmed as HD 20794 d. He was analysing archive data recorded by the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3990c4f6d8a65ba9\">>>", "published": "January 29, 2025", "siteName": "www.skyatnightmagazine.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"34b69b9b87e285b7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSearch for life: This newly discovered super Earth outside our solar system marks a significant milestone - BusinessToday\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"34b69b9b87e285b7\">>>", "url": "https://www.businesstoday.in/science/story/search-for-life-this-newly-discovered-super-earth-outside-our-solar-system-marks-a-significant-milestone-463951-2025-02-09", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0014e89da42f2ab9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 d, with a mass six times that of Earth, <strong>orbits a star similar to our sun</strong>. The planet’s location within the habitable zone — where conditions may allow liquid water to exist — offers scientists a compelling target for future ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0014e89da42f2ab9\">>>", "published": "February 10, 2025", "siteName": "www.businesstoday.in"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1188482a4870a7be\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExistence Of Exoplanet HD 20794 d In A Habitable Zone Confirmed - Astrobiology\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1188482a4870a7be\">>>", "url": "https://astrobiology.com/2025/01/existence-of-exoplanet-hd-20794-d-in-a-habitable-zone-confirmed.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f39e7835c1dae2e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>Dr Michael Cretignier first identified a candidate exoplanet signal in 2022</strong>, while analysing archived data recorded by the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8f39e7835c1dae2e\">>>", "published": "January 28, 2025", "siteName": "astrobiology.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4dd43d7eddffcb07\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEvidence for at least three planet candidates orbiting HD 20794 | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4dd43d7eddffcb07\">>>", "url": "https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2017/09/aa30406-17/aa30406-17.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6ae538cc0d09f3c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThere is also weak evidence for the existence of signals at periods of 43 and 11 d. While the 43 d signal does not pass the Bayes factor criterion, the inclusion of this signal in the model can reduce the eccentricity of the 89 d signal. Although the 11 d signal only increases the Bayes factor by a factor of about 20, it consistently appears in different data chunks. Thus by applying noise modeling to the P11 and newer HARPS data, we confirm the two candidates at periods of 18 and 90 d reported by P11 and quantify them better. But we are suspicious about the existence of the reported 40 d candidate because it does not pass the signal detection criteria.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e6ae538cc0d09f3c\">>>", "published": "September 18, 2017", "siteName": "www.aanda.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"931f540cc80544d7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGravity Simulator | HD 20794 - System With 4 Exoplanets\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"931f540cc80544d7\">>>", "url": "https://gravitysimulator.org/exoplanets/hd-20794-system-with-4-exoplanets/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5ffc2cc3b27fdc0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>3D visualisation and gravity simulation of the exoplanetary system HD 20794, which contains 4 exoplanets and was discovered by the La Silla Observatory</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5ffc2cc3b27fdc0\">>>", "siteName": "gravitysimulator.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43d3cf0c8e551780\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe HARPS search for Earth-like planets in the habitable zone. I. Very low-mass planets around HD 20794, HD 85512, and HD 192310 | Request PDF\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"43d3cf0c8e551780\">>>", "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/253183556_The_HARPS_search_for_Earth-like_planets_in_the_habitable_zone_I_Very_low-mass_planets_around_HD_20794_HD_85512_and_HD_192310", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3340d0b368bc880e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>For the outer planet, we find an eccentricity of 0.45 −0.11 +0.10</strong> , whereas the inner planets are compatible with circular orbits. The latter is likely to be a rocky planet in the habitable zone of HD 20794.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3340d0b368bc880e\">>>", "published": "February 21, 2025", "siteName": "www.researchgate.net"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f8ab8eba02aa5b33\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSuper-Earth found just 20 light-years away is our 'best chance so far' to find life\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f8ab8eba02aa5b33\">>>", "url": "https://www.earth.com/news/super-earth-hd-20794-d-found-just-20-light-years-away-is-best-target-yet-for-life/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54e60d0a9b4c652e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOxford University scientist Dr. Michael Cretignier first noticed something unusual in this star’s light while examining archived data from the HARPS spectrograph on the 3.6-meter telescope at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54e60d0a9b4c652e\">>>", "published": "November 30, 2025", "siteName": "www.earth.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c8e93ce70a3fcbc3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExploring HD 20794 d: A Super-Earth Laboratory for Habitability\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c8e93ce70a3fcbc3\">>>", "url": "https://www.seti.org/news/exploring-hd-20794-d-a-super-earth-laboratory-for-habitability/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3a3575763696657e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThese instruments, used over a period of more than 20 years, allowed astronomers to confirm the presence of HD 20794 d alongside two other planets in the same system. One of the most intriguing aspects of HD 20794 d is its <strong>highly eccentric orbit</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3a3575763696657e\">>>", "published": "June 17, 2025", "siteName": "www.seti.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775298797746}}
