{"type": "message", "id": "2ddc06e4", "parentId": "565f6b9b", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:33:45.523Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I found that HD 20794 d was originally discovered in 2011 using the radial velocity method. However, looking at the 2025 paper, the outer planet has an eccentricity of 0.45. But wait - the 2025 paper is about a planet with a period of 647.6 days, which is different from the original HD 20794 d discovered in 2011 with a period of about 90 days.\n\nLet me search for more information about the original discovery and its eccentricity."}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "functions.web_search:18", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "exoplanets radial velocity high eccentricity discovered before 2020 less than 5 Earth masses 100 days period", "count": 10}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "modelstudio", "model": "kimi-k2.5", "usage": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 0, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775298815721, "responseId": "chatcmpl-8f713444-63ea-9382-853a-ceec14fd4674"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "e6c25ffb", "parentId": "2ddc06e4", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T10:33:46.890Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:18", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"exoplanets radial velocity high eccentricity discovered before 2020 less than 5 Earth masses 100 days period\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 1364,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db9e4756ea2e88d5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanets detected by radial velocity - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db9e4756ea2e88d5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanets_detected_by_radial_velocity\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e35d73ce9191968b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n9.4 times the mass of Jupiter); the least massive confirmed planet is Gliese 581 e, which masses 0.007906 MJ or 2.51 M🜨. The longest period of any confirmed exoplanet is <strong>55 Cancri d</strong>, which takes 5169 days or 14.15 years to make one trip around the star; the shortest period is Gliese 876 ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e35d73ce9191968b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 3, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c25fb401480b541b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c25fb401480b541b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/539/2/727/8098228\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f17418e1e0eddf67\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nABSTRACT. We examine the eccentricity distribution(s) of radial velocity (RV) detected exoplanets. Previously, the eccentricity distribution was found to b\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f17418e1e0eddf67\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 12, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7fe4b19cf10e57fd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of exoplanet extremes - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7fe4b19cf10e57fd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanet_extremes\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b75f4deb7421f9c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe following are lists of extremes among the known exoplanets. The properties listed here are those for which values are known reliably. The study of exoplanets is one of the most dynamic emerging fields of science, thus these values may change as new discoveries are made.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9b75f4deb7421f9c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"1 month ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"864305e57ea0972e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGiant Outer Transiting Exoplanet Mass (GOT ‘EM) Survey. II. Discovery of a Failed Hot Jupiter on a 2.7 Yr, Highly Eccentric Orbit* | Request PDF\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"864305e57ea0972e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354732066_Giant_Outer_Transiting_Exoplanet_Mass_GOT_'EM_Survey_II_Discovery_of_a_Failed_Hot_Jupiter_on_a_27_Yr_Highly_Eccentric_Orbit\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"004714d45675ebf9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis supports the hypothesis that dynamical interactions with wide stellar companions plays an important role in the formation of highly eccentric exoplanets. ... Paul A. Dalba · Heather A. Knutson ... The observed correlation between outer giant planets and inner super-Earths is emerging as an important constraint on planet formation theories. In this study we focus on Kepler-167, which is currently the only system known to contain both inner transiting super-Earths and a confirmed outer transiting gas giant companion beyond 1 au. Using long term radial velocity monitoring, we measure the mass of the gas giant Kepler-167e (P = 1071 days) to be 1.01^(+0.16)_(−0.15) M_J, thus confirming it as a Jupiter analog.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"004714d45675ebf9\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 1, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb6c527250777f4b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDetermining the true mass of radial-velocity exoplanets with Gaia - Nine planet candidates in the brown dwarf or stellar regime and 27 confirmed planets | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb6c527250777f4b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2021/01/aa39168-20/aa39168-20.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42525ef770555d56\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe also confirm the planetary nature of 27 exoplanets, including HD 10180 c, d and g. Studying the orbital periods, eccentricities, and host-star metallicities in the BD domain, we found distributions with respect to true masses consistent with other publications. The distribution of orbital periods shows of a void of BD detections below ~100 d, while eccentricity and metallicity distributions agree with a transition between BDs similar to planets and BDs similar to stars in the range 40–50 MJ.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"42525ef770555d56\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 21, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aanda.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dabc4f5400cd8df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExoplanets Catalogue Analysis: The Distribution of Exoplanets at FGK Stars by Mass and Orbital Period Accounting for the Observational Selection in the Radial Velocity Method | MDPI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dabc4f5400cd8df\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4433/14/2/353\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"147d828ed5449977\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIf this fraction of the orbit is small, the Kepler curve degenerates into a linear or quadratic drift of the star’s radial velocity, which indicates the presence of long-periodic bodies in the system, but does not allow their period and mass to be determined. For example, planets with P/T &gt; 2.5 (HD 221420 b, Pr0211 c, HAT-P-17 c, HR 5183 b, HD 190984 b, and HD 133131 B b) are in highly eccentric orbits.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"147d828ed5449977\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdpi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7ee08cf1723f0362\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7ee08cf1723f0362\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.20385\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"546a531efde40196\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHelp | Advanced Search · arXiv is a free distribution service and an open-access archive for nearly 2.4 million scholarly articles in the fields of physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative finance, statistics, electrical engineering and systems science, and ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"546a531efde40196\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef18c92899ea49a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDiscoveries of exoplanets - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ef18c92899ea49a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discoveries_of_exoplanets\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"264e0e136df33485\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe planet orbits its parent star ... minimum mass estimated at 1.9 times that of Earth. As of January 2010, this is the lightest known extrasolar planet to orbit a main-sequence star. 30 planets: On October 19, it was announced that 30 new planets were discovered, all were detected by the radial velocity method. It is the most planets ever announced in a single day during the exoplanet ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"264e0e136df33485\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"2 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d01141c1fab0d0c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGJ 367b: A dense, ultrashort-period sub-Earth planet transiting a nearby red dwarf star | Science\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3d01141c1fab0d0c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aay3253\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"69941d61d3708f84\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPrecise masses and radii of USP exoplanets could provide constraints on their unknown formation and evolution processes. We report the detection and characterization of the USP planet <strong>GJ 367b</strong> using high-precision photometry and radial velocity ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"69941d61d3708f84\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.science.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2907de8b93fd886f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEccentric Jupiter - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2907de8b93fd886f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eccentric_Jupiter\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b1e83d012f66675f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSome of the detected &quot;eccentric planets&quot; may actually be multiple planets with near-circular orbits. The majority of eccentric planets have been reported based on radial velocity measurements using Doppler spectroscopy by which eccentricity is directly measurable.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b1e83d012f66675f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 26, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "exoplanets radial velocity high eccentricity discovered before 2020 less than 5 Earth masses 100 days period", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 1364, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"db9e4756ea2e88d5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nList of exoplanets detected by radial velocity - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"db9e4756ea2e88d5\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanets_detected_by_radial_velocity", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e35d73ce9191968b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n9.4 times the mass of Jupiter); the least massive confirmed planet is Gliese 581 e, which masses 0.007906 MJ or 2.51 M🜨. The longest period of any confirmed exoplanet is <strong>55 Cancri d</strong>, which takes 5169 days or 14.15 years to make one trip around the star; the shortest period is Gliese 876 ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e35d73ce9191968b\">>>", "published": "December 3, 2024", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c25fb401480b541b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best | Monthly Notices of the Royal Astronomical Society | Oxford Academic\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c25fb401480b541b\">>>", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/539/2/727/8098228", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f17418e1e0eddf67\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nABSTRACT. We examine the eccentricity distribution(s) of radial velocity (RV) detected exoplanets. Previously, the eccentricity distribution was found to b\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f17418e1e0eddf67\">>>", "published": "April 12, 2025", "siteName": "academic.oup.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7fe4b19cf10e57fd\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nList of exoplanet extremes - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7fe4b19cf10e57fd\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_exoplanet_extremes", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b75f4deb7421f9c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe following are lists of extremes among the known exoplanets. The properties listed here are those for which values are known reliably. The study of exoplanets is one of the most dynamic emerging fields of science, thus these values may change as new discoveries are made.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9b75f4deb7421f9c\">>>", "published": "1 month ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"864305e57ea0972e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGiant Outer Transiting Exoplanet Mass (GOT ‘EM) Survey. II. Discovery of a Failed Hot Jupiter on a 2.7 Yr, Highly Eccentric Orbit* | Request PDF\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"864305e57ea0972e\">>>", "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354732066_Giant_Outer_Transiting_Exoplanet_Mass_GOT_'EM_Survey_II_Discovery_of_a_Failed_Hot_Jupiter_on_a_27_Yr_Highly_Eccentric_Orbit", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"004714d45675ebf9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis supports the hypothesis that dynamical interactions with wide stellar companions plays an important role in the formation of highly eccentric exoplanets. ... Paul A. Dalba · Heather A. Knutson ... The observed correlation between outer giant planets and inner super-Earths is emerging as an important constraint on planet formation theories. In this study we focus on Kepler-167, which is currently the only system known to contain both inner transiting super-Earths and a confirmed outer transiting gas giant companion beyond 1 au. Using long term radial velocity monitoring, we measure the mass of the gas giant Kepler-167e (P = 1071 days) to be 1.01^(+0.16)_(−0.15) M_J, thus confirming it as a Jupiter analog.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"004714d45675ebf9\">>>", "published": "October 1, 2021", "siteName": "www.researchgate.net"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fb6c527250777f4b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDetermining the true mass of radial-velocity exoplanets with Gaia - Nine planet candidates in the brown dwarf or stellar regime and 27 confirmed planets | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fb6c527250777f4b\">>>", "url": "https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2021/01/aa39168-20/aa39168-20.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"42525ef770555d56\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWe also confirm the planetary nature of 27 exoplanets, including HD 10180 c, d and g. Studying the orbital periods, eccentricities, and host-star metallicities in the BD domain, we found distributions with respect to true masses consistent with other publications. The distribution of orbital periods shows of a void of BD detections below ~100 d, while eccentricity and metallicity distributions agree with a transition between BDs similar to planets and BDs similar to stars in the range 40–50 MJ.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"42525ef770555d56\">>>", "published": "December 21, 2020", "siteName": "www.aanda.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5dabc4f5400cd8df\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nExoplanets Catalogue Analysis: The Distribution of Exoplanets at FGK Stars by Mass and Orbital Period Accounting for the Observational Selection in the Radial Velocity Method | MDPI\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5dabc4f5400cd8df\">>>", "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4433/14/2/353", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"147d828ed5449977\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIf this fraction of the orbit is small, the Kepler curve degenerates into a linear or quadratic drift of the star’s radial velocity, which indicates the presence of long-periodic bodies in the system, but does not allow their period and mass to be determined. For example, planets with P/T &gt; 2.5 (HD 221420 b, Pr0211 c, HAT-P-17 c, HR 5183 b, HD 190984 b, and HD 133131 B b) are in highly eccentric orbits.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"147d828ed5449977\">>>", "published": "February 10, 2023", "siteName": "www.mdpi.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7ee08cf1723f0362\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRV-exoplanet eccentricities: Good, Beta, and Best\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7ee08cf1723f0362\">>>", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2503.20385", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"546a531efde40196\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHelp | Advanced Search · arXiv is a free distribution service and an open-access archive for nearly 2.4 million scholarly articles in the fields of physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative finance, statistics, electrical engineering and systems science, and ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"546a531efde40196\">>>", "siteName": "arxiv.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ef18c92899ea49a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDiscoveries of exoplanets - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ef18c92899ea49a\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discoveries_of_exoplanets", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"264e0e136df33485\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe planet orbits its parent star ... minimum mass estimated at 1.9 times that of Earth. As of January 2010, this is the lightest known extrasolar planet to orbit a main-sequence star. 30 planets: On October 19, it was announced that 30 new planets were discovered, all were detected by the radial velocity method. It is the most planets ever announced in a single day during the exoplanet ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"264e0e136df33485\">>>", "published": "2 weeks ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d01141c1fab0d0c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGJ 367b: A dense, ultrashort-period sub-Earth planet transiting a nearby red dwarf star | Science\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3d01141c1fab0d0c\">>>", "url": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aay3253", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"69941d61d3708f84\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nPrecise masses and radii of USP exoplanets could provide constraints on their unknown formation and evolution processes. We report the detection and characterization of the USP planet <strong>GJ 367b</strong> using high-precision photometry and radial velocity ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"69941d61d3708f84\">>>", "siteName": "www.science.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2907de8b93fd886f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEccentric Jupiter - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2907de8b93fd886f\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eccentric_Jupiter", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b1e83d012f66675f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSome of the detected &quot;eccentric planets&quot; may actually be multiple planets with near-circular orbits. The majority of eccentric planets have been reported based on radial velocity measurements using Doppler spectroscopy by which eccentricity is directly measurable.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b1e83d012f66675f\">>>", "published": "October 26, 2025", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775298826889}}
