ute gravitational influence of the planet on its host star</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"efc7e418a02d1dc5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 31, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"bytebridge.medium.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7557425f5ca513df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n82 G. Eridani d - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7557425f5ca513df\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/82_G._Eridani_d\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df3a1687b40fd907\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n82 G. Eridani d (HD 20794 d) is an exoplanet, possibly rocky, orbiting the solar-type star 82 G. Eridani. It is <strong>at least five times more massive than Earth</strong> and has an orbit partially within the habitable zone of its host star. Depending on its physical characteristics, which are poorly known, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"df3a1687b40fd907\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"2 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78dc68e5625ab932\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRevisiting the multi-planetary system of the nearby star HD 20794 - Confirmation of a low-mass planet in the habitable zone of a nearby G-dwarf | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78dc68e5625ab932\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2025/01/aa51769-24/aa51769-24.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c9d12ece0a4f8f5b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe confirm the presence of three planets, with periods of 18.3142 ± 0.0022 d, 89.68 ± 0.10 d, and 647.6−2.7+2.5 d, along with masses of 2.15 ± 0.17 M⊕, 2.98 ± 0.29 M⊕, and 5.82 ± 0.57 M⊕ respectively. For the outer planet, we find an eccentricity of <strong>0.45−0.11+0.10</strong>, whereas the ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c9d12ece0a4f8f5b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 28, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aanda.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d4e7b8ca292e383b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n82 G. Eridani - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d4e7b8ca292e383b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HD_20794\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8127987cca39b5df\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nData for the research was gathered at the High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher spectrograph at La Silla Observatory in Chile. With the discovery, HD 20794 d became the <strong>12th-closest potentially habitable planet to Earth</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8127987cca39b5df\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 19, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd38f7c6b85b32e0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHD 20794 d\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd38f7c6b85b32e0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"http://www.exoplanetkyoto.org/exohtml/HD_20794_d.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f2ae1297f7ab27bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDisplay orbital revolution of HD 20794 d around the hoststar HD 20794\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f2ae1297f7ab27bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.exoplanetkyoto.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a2a48460a4288bd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Super-Earth to Test the Limits of Habitability - Universe Today\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a2a48460a4288bd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.universetoday.com/articles/a-super-earth-to-test-the-limits-of-habitability\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"98c7ff0f0769204b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n&quot;The orbital period of HD 20794 d resides both in the optimistic and conservative HZ,&quot; the authors write in their research. &quot;This is an interesting result because we do not have many examples of planets with M &lt; 10 Earth masses with mass measurement from RVs in the HZ of Sun-like stars.&quot; The planet travels between the inner edge of its star&#x27;s HZ (0.75 AU) and outside of it (2 AU) as it follows its eccentric orbit.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"98c7ff0f0769204b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 13, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.universetoday.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a8042f7f9fc673ea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAstronomy:82 G. Eridani - HandWiki\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a8042f7f9fc673ea\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://handwiki.org/wiki/Astronomy:82_G._Eridani\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a8d6917725135a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nData for the research was gathered at the High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher spectrograph at La Silla Observatory in Chile.[21] With the discovery, HD 20794 d became the <strong>12th-closest potentially habitable planet to Earth</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"28a8d6917725135a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 6, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"handwiki.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b632558efbb78420\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExoplanet HD 20794 d in the habitable zone | BBC Sky at Night Magazine\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b632558efbb78420\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.skyatnightmagazine.com/news/hd-20794-d\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"544242fbcb6a2e21\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDr Michael Cretignier from the University of Oxford in the UK first discovered the exoplanet candidate that would later be confirmed as HD 20794 d. He was analysing archive data recorded by the HARPS (High Accuracy Radial Velocity Planet Searcher) spectrograph at the La Silla Observatory in Chile.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"544242fbcb6a2e21\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 29, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.skyatnightmagazine.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a11989576cdaaf5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRevisiting the Multi-planetary System of the Nearby star HD 20794: Confirmation of a Low-mass Planet in the Habitable Zone of a Nearby G-dwarf - Astrobiology\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a11989576cdaaf5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://astrobiology.com/2025/02/revisiting-the-multi-planetary-system-of-the-nearby-star-hd-20794-confirmation-of-a-low-mass-planet-in-the-habitable-zone-of-a-nearby-g-dwarf.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"405552a3dcc0c6be\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor the outer planet, we find an eccentricity of <strong>0.45 +/- 0.10</strong>, whereas the inner planets are compatible with circular orbits. The latter is likely to be a rocky planet in the habitable zone of HD 20794.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"405552a3dcc0c6be\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 4, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"astrobiology.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"HD 20794 d\" mass 4.8 Earth eccentricity discovery 2011 radial velocity", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 856, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e6a0d71121182d7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHD 20794 d - NASA Science\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e6a0d71121182d7\">>>", "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanet-catalog/hd-20794-d/", "description": "\n