D 20794c in\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a47ea7aa13faf88b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 21, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"270782f13f09d3ea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe HARPS search for Earth-like planets in the habitable zone - I. Very low-mass planets around HD 20794, HD 85512, and HD 192310 | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"270782f13f09d3ea\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2011/10/aa17055-11/aa17055-11.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4394ad4424c10dc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n) has been computed in accordance with Lovis et al. (2011b). Finally, the stellar rotation period Prot(R′vHK) and the estimated stellar age are both computed from ... The raw radial-velocity data of the star HD 20794 are presented in Table 7 and shown in Fig.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a4394ad4424c10dc\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 3, 2011\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.aanda.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6946a9fb4b4209d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHD 20794 | NASA Exoplanet Archive\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6946a9fb4b4209d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu/overview/HD%2020794\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"033332930ada280a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe HARPS search for Earth-like planets in the habitable zone:I -- Very low-mass planets around HD20794, HD85512 and HD192310 Pepe et al. 2011 | Reference Overview\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"033332930ada280a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"exoplanetarchive.ipac.caltech.edu\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Pepe 2011 HD 20794 d eccentricity 0.4 radial velocity HARPS", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 911, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b4e280abbc8e3d90\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA&A 534, A58 (2011) DOI: 10.1051/0004-6361/201117055 c⃝ESO 2011 Astronomy &\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b4e280abbc8e3d90\">>>", "url": "https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/pdf/2011/10/aa17055-11.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7a904acce8ea4b0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nF. Pepe et al.: The HARPS search for Earth-like planets in the habitable zone. I. Fig. 22. Top: residuals of the radial velocities of HD 20794 to the three-\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c7a904acce8ea4b0\">>>", "siteName": "www.aanda.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6bb7d6c5e0194abc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEvidence for at least three planet candidates orbiting HD 20794 | Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6bb7d6c5e0194abc\">>>", "url": "https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2017/09/aa30406-17/aa30406-17.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1fb437b053e7d179\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn this work, we apply this noise model framework to the HARPS RV measurements of HD 20794. HD 20794 is a <strong>high-velocity and metal-deficient G8 star</strong> with a mass of ... 0.018 M⊙ (Ramírez et al. 2013). It has been reported to host at least three planets and a dust disk (Pepe et al.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1fb437b053e7d179\">>>", "published": "September 18, 2017", "siteName": "www.aanda.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d4b491d4d16fcd5b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVizieR Online Data Catalog: HD20794, HD85512, HD192310 HARPS radial velocities (Pepe+, 2011) - ADS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d4b491d4d16fcd5b\">>>", "url": "https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2011yCat.