TED_CONTENT id=\"b037197fa7df2ab9\">>>", "siteName": "arxiv.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ff86367d110c1a36\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n82 G. Eridani d - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ff86367d110c1a36\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/82_G._Eridani_d", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"892a734342f5e439\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn addition to planet d, 82 G. Eridani also hosts two other planets in closer orbits: 82 G. Eridani b, which is a likely super-Earth with an orbital period of 18 days and a minimum mass of 2.15±0.17 M🜨, and 82 G. Eridani c, also likely a super-Earth, with an orbital period of 89 days and a minimum mass of 2.98±0.29 M🜨. All of them were discovered by doppler spectroscopy, with planets b and c being discovered in 2011 by F. Pepe et al.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"892a734342f5e439\">>>", "published": "2 weeks ago", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a132f4244e2532c7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nRevisiting the Multi-planetary System of the Nearby star HD 20794: Confirmation of a Low-mass Planet in the Habitable Zone of a Nearby G-dwarf - Astrobiology\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a132f4244e2532c7\">>>", "url": "https://astrobiology.com/2025/02/revisiting-the-multi-planetary-system-of-the-nearby-star-hd-20794-confirmation-of-a-low-mass-planet-in-the-habitable-zone-of-a-nearby-g-dwarf.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cbede97ece5f1a6a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nWe confirm the presence of three ... 2.98 +/- 0.29 MEarth, and 5.82 +/- 0.57 MEarth respectively. <strong>For the outer planet, we find an eccentricity of 0.45 +/- 0.10</strong>, whereas the inner planets are compatible with circular ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cbede97ece5f1a6a\">>>", "published": "February 4, 2025", "siteName": "astrobiology.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"